 75GA    76GE(D,3HE):XUNDL-1           2009KA06,2008KAZT                  200905
 75GA c  Includes {+76}Ge(pol d,{+3}He)                                         
 75GA c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2009Ka06:                          
 75GA2c  Phys Rev C 79, 021301(R) (2009); and 2008KaZT: private communication   
 75GA3c  received from B.P. Kay et al., Argonne National Lab, Dec 2, 2008       
 75GA c  2008KaZT contains data details for eight different reactions.          
 75GA c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster): Dec 11, 2008.                         
 75GA c  Edited by B. Singh, Jan 14, 2009 in response to some                   
 75GA2c  corrected VAP values received from 2008KaZT                            
 75GA c  Edited by B. Singh, April 28, 2009 to include 2009Ka06 reference       
 75GA c  E=80 MeV beam provided by the AVF cyclotron at RCNP, Osaka. Enriched   
 75GA2c  target. Vector-polarized 80-MeV deuteron beam with A{-y}=0.520 {I10}.  
 75GA3c  {+3}He outgoing particles detected and analyzed with Grand Raiden      
 75GA4c  magnetic spectrograph, with an angular aperture of |+1.1|'. FWHM=50 keV
 75GA c  Measured precise absolute cross sections and relative cross sections   
 75GA2c  where these are maximum for the relevant L transfer, angular           
 75GA3c  distributions and polarization asymmetries. Vector analyzing powers    
 75GA4c  were deduced from the measured polarization asymmetries by dividing    
 75GA5c  by a factor of 1.04 (2*[beam vector polarization=0.520 {I10}]).        
 75GA6c  Spectroscopic factors were deduced from analysis of cross              
 75GA7c  section data by DWBA calculations using PTOLEMY code and six           
 75GA8c  different sets of optical-model potential parameters and two           
 75GA9c  bound-state potential parameters.                                      
 75GA c  Single-particle transfer reactions studied in 2008KaZT:                
 75GA2c  {+74}Ge(d,{+3}He){+73}Ga; {+76}Ge(d,{+3}He){+75}Ga;                    
 75GA3c  {+76}Se(d,{+3}He){+75}As; {+78}Se(d,{+3}He){+77}As;                    
 75GA4c  {+74}Ge({+3}He,d){+75}As; {+76}Ge({+3}He,d){+77}As;                    
 75GA5c  {+76}Se({+3}He,d){+77}Br; {+78}Se({+3}He,d){+79}Br.                    
 75GA6c  For (d,{+3}He) reactions, polarized deuteron beam is also used to      
 75GA7c  obtain asymmetries and subsequent information about parities of levels.
 75GA8c  See relevant dataset in XUNDL database for each reaction.              
 75GA c  The experiments were designed to map out the occupancies of valence    
 75GA2c  proton orbitals in the ground states of {+74}Ge, {+76}Ge, {+76}Se and  
 75GA3c  {+78}Se by precise measurements of absolute cross sections and relative
 75GA4c  cross sections at the angles where these are maximum in angular        
 75GA5c  distributions in single-particle transfer reactions.                   
 75GA c  Uncertainty in cross sections: statistical uncertainty of 1%           
 75GA2c  for strong peaks; systematic uncertainties of 5% in absolute values    
 75GA3c  and 3% in relative values. Multiplets have larger uncertainties        
 75GA c  ENSDF database available at: http://www.nndc.bnl.gov/ensdf/            
 75GA c  All data are from 2008KaZT unless otherwise stated                     
 75GA cL E,J$ Unless otherwise noted, 2008KaZT take values from 'adopted levels,
 75GA2cL gammas' dataset for {+75}Ga in the ENSDF database                      
 75GA cL E(X)$ 178 and 229 groups are unresolved, angle-to-angle ratios of      
 75GA2cL cross sections used to assign separate cross sections. See details     
 75GA3cL of the fitting procedure for unresolved peaks in 2008KaZT              
 75GA cL E(Y)$ 1508 and 1545 groups are unresolved, line-shape fitting method   
 75GA2cL was used to assign separate cross sections. See details of the fitting 
 75GA3cL procedure for unresolved peaks in 2008KaZT                             
 75GA cL J(B)$ From measured polarization asymmetry in 2008KaZT                 
 75GA cL L$ 2008KaZT relied on the assignment of L transfers                    
 75GA2cL in previous studies (see ENSDF database for {+75}Ga). These assignments
 75GA3cL were, nevertheless, confirmed in 2008KaZT from their measured          
 75GA4cL angle-to-angle ratios                                                  
 75GA CL S$LABEL=C2S                                                            
 75GA cL S$ From 2008KaZT. The spectroscopic factors were deduced for different 
 75GA2cL L transfers as follows: 4.5|' data for L=1, 8|' data for L=3, and 12|' 
 75GA3cL data for L=4. The values are the ratios of experimental cross sections 
 75GA4cL and calculated DWBA cross sections using the finite-range PTOLEMY code.
 75GA5cL The normalization procedure is described in 2008KaZT. Six different    
 75GA6cL sets of optical-model potential parameters and two different           
 75GA7cL bound-state potential parameters were used for the calculations. See   
 75GA8cL 2008KaZT for listing of these parameters. Differences in C{+2}S values 
 75GA9cL were less than 10% for different sets of optical parameters used.      
 75GAAcL The effects of the bound-state parameters were also within the         
 75GABcL uncertainties.                                                         
